# ACL for the cluster test. The username of each client is its node id (MQTT_USERNAME={node}).
# Payloads are ciphertext / authenticated end to end, so the broker is not trusted; these rules only stop a node from
# impersonating another node's presence or reading someone else's inbox.
#
# Mosquitto applies `topic` lines that appear BEFORE the first `user` line to anonymous clients only, so every node gets
# its own block. Copy a block for each node id in NODES (and keep NET_ID as the "+" level, or replace it with the id).
#
#   read  presence of everyone (retained + last-will)        write only its own presence
#   read  only its own inbox / audio                          write into any peer's inbox / audio

user bot-1
topic read zi/v1/+/presence/+
topic write zi/v1/+/presence/bot-1
topic read zi/v1/+/node/bot-1/in
topic read zi/v1/+/node/bot-1/au
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/in
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/au

user yt-1
topic read zi/v1/+/presence/+
topic write zi/v1/+/presence/yt-1
topic read zi/v1/+/node/yt-1/in
topic read zi/v1/+/node/yt-1/au
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/in
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/au

user tts-1
topic read zi/v1/+/presence/+
topic write zi/v1/+/presence/tts-1
topic read zi/v1/+/node/tts-1/in
topic read zi/v1/+/node/tts-1/au
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/in
topic write zi/v1/+/node/+/au
